  "findings": [
    "Full original scope macros/labels/root/count and eight enum indices match the selected native C/C++ scope declarations. Disabled admission returns true before lookup; unknown enabled scopes return false; Apply delegates only to a found policy.",
    "The six original concrete policy constructions remain FS, child process, worker, inspector, WASI, addon. Eight map insertions retain their original grouped order and shared policy identity. The pinned libc++ make_shared delegates to allocate_shared; the admitted stateless allocator has no construct override, so this uses the same normal control-block/allocator_traits construction path.",
    "The original five simple policies keep deny_all_=true on Apply and is_granted as deny_all_==false. Their complete actual headers and implementation bodies were read.",
    "FS Apply retains wildcard early return, its original read-versus-else write state branch, ordered PathResolve calls, GrantAccess's real physical directory expansion, conditional tree insertion, and deny flag publication. No alternate policy was introduced for a scope the original dispatcher does not normally select.",
    "Windows is_tree_granted retains sequential device, UNC, and slash prefix removals before Lookup(..., true). Original empty-tree and end-node tests, parent-prefix accounting, wildcard precedence, and lookup bounds are preserved.",
    "Insert retains original substr(parent_node_prefix_len, i), CreateChild before wildcard child, and parent prefix update. CreateChild retains operator[] null entry publication, actual native CHECK, prefix split/copy/reassign/allocation/publication and recursive decision order; CreateWildcardChild, NextNode and IsEndNode match the original decision bodies.",
    "Required Debug inputs remain explicit. This peer reads only the pre-Debug Insert algorithm and does not qualify EnabledDebugList, SPrintF/FWrite or native output.",
    "Pure source comparison of 28 selected decisions/bodies/macros passed after only the documented type/namespace, borrowed Environment parameter, native assertion, and allocate_shared adapter substitutions. Full original and current files were read; no compilation or runtime."
